<p><strong>Experience It: Values in a Single Image</strong></p>
<p>Choose one of the six works in the Gallery above, the one you react to most strongly. Spend two full minutes with it before you answer.</p>
<ol>
<li>What is the first thing you feel when you look at it? Write one sentence about that feeling.</li>
<li>Now describe the work's structure: what is large, what is small, where does your eye travel, and what is it not allowed to rest on?</li>
<li>What value (justice, grief, dignity, freedom, peace, fear) does the work make visible, and which choices in its form make you say so?</li>
</ol>
</div></div>
